{
  "title": "Dua for Fulfillment of Wishes",
  "data": "Dua of Insistence\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ السَّمٰوَاتِ السَّبْعِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُنَّ\nALLAAHUMMA RABBAS SAMAAWAATIS SAB'I WA MAA BAYNAHUNN\nO Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what is between them,\nوَرَبَّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nWA RABBAL A'RSHIL A'ZEEM\nand Lord of the Mighty Throne,\nوَرَبَّ جَبْرَئِيْلَ وَمِيْكَاۤئِيْلَ وَاِسْرَافِيْلَ\nWA RABBA JABRA'EELA WA MEEKAA'EELA WA ISRAAFEEL\nand Lord of Jibra'il, Mika'il, and Israfil,\nوَرَبَّ الْقُرْاٰنِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nWA RABBAL QUR'AANIL A'ZEEM\nand Lord of the Great Qur'an,\nوَرَبَّ مُحَمَّدٍ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nWA RABBA MUHAMMADIN KHAATAMIN NABIYYEEN\nand Lord of Muhammad, the Seal of the Prophets,\nاِنِّىْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِالَّذِىْ تَقُوْمُ بِهِ السَّمَاۤءُ وَبِهٖ تَقُوْمُ الْاَرْضُ\nINNEE AS'ALUKA BILLADHEE TAQOOMU BIHIS SAMAA'U WA BIHEE TAQOOMUL ARD\nverily I ask You by that through which the sky stands and through which the earth stands,\nوَبِهٖ تُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ الْجَمْعِ وَبِهٖ تَجْمَعُ بَيْنَ الْمُتَفَرِّقِ\nWA BIHEE TUFARRIQU BAYNAL JAM'I WA BIHEE TAJMA'U BAYNAL MUTAFARRIQ\nand through which You separate what is joined and join what is separated,\nوَبِهٖ تَرْزُقُ الْاَحْياۤءَ\nWA BIHEE TARZUQUL AHYAA'\nand through which You give sustenance to the living,\nوَبِهٖ اَحْصَيْتَ عَدَدَ الرِّمَالِ وَوَزْنَ الْجِبَالِ وَكَيْلَ الْبُحُوْرِ\nWA BIHEE AHSAYTA A'DADAR RIMAALI WA WAZNAL JIBAALI WA KAYLAL BUHOOR\nand through which You have counted the number of the sands, the weight of the mountains, and the measure of the seas.\n\nHaving said this, invoke Allah's blessings upon the Holy Prophet and his Household and submit your request, preferably insistently.",
  "tabs": [
    "Dua Allahumma Imla' Qalbi\nAfter the fourth unit of the Night Prayer, or in the Watr prayer, recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ امْلَاءْ قَلْبِىْ حُبًّا لَكَ وَخَشْيَةً مِنْكَ\nALLAAHUMMAM LA' QALBEE HUBBAN LAKA WA KHASHYATAN MINK\nO Allah, fill my heart with love for You and awe of You,\nوَتَصْدِيْقًا وَاِيْمَانًا بِكَ\nWA TASDEEQAN WA EEMAANAN BIK\nwith belief and faith in You,\nوَفَرَقًا مِنْكَ وَشَوْقًا اِلَيْكَ\nWA FARAQAN MINKA WA SHAWQAN ILAYK\nwith fear of You and longing for You,\nيَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ\nYAA DHAL JALAALI WAL IKRAAM\nO Lord of Majesty and Honor.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ حَبِّبْ اِلَیَّ لِقَاۤئَكَ\nALLAAHUMMA HABBIB ILAYYA LIQAA'AK\nO Allah, make meeting You beloved to me,\nوَاجْعَلْ لِىْ فِىْ لِقَاۤئِكَ خَيْرَ الرَّحْمَةِ وَالْبَرَكَةِ\nWAJ'AL LEE FEE LIQAA'IKA KHAYRAR RAHMATI WAL BARAKAH\nand place for me, in meeting You, the best of mercy and blessing.\nوَاَلْحِقْنِىْ بِالصَّالِحِيْنَ وَلَا تُؤَخِّرْنِىْ مَعَ الْاَشْرَارِ\nWA ALHIQNEE BIS SAALIHEENA WA LAA TU'AKHKHIRNEE MA'AL ASHRAAR\nJoin me with the righteous and do not hold me back with the wicked;\nوَاَلْحِقْنِىْ بِصَالِحِ مَنْ مَضٰى وَاجْعَلْنِىْ مَعَ صَالِحِ مَنْ بَقِىَ\nWA ALHIQNEE BISAALIHI MAN MADAA WAJ'ALNEE MA'A SAALIHI MAN BAQEE\njoin me with the righteous who have passed, and place me with the righteous who remain;\nوَخُذْ بِىْ سَبِيْلَ الصَّالِحِيْنَ\nWA KHUDH BEE SABEELAS SAALIHEEN\ntake me along the path of the righteous,\nوَاَعِنِّىْ عَلٰى نَفْسِىْ بِمَا تُعِيْنُ بِهِ الصَّالِحِيْنَ عَلٰۤى اَنْفُسِهِمْ\nWA A'INNEE A'LAA NAFSEE BIMAA TU'EENU BIHIS SAALIHEENA A'LAA ANFUSIHIM\nand help me against my soul with that by which You help the righteous against their souls.\nوَلَا تَرُدَّنِىْ فِىْ سُوْۤءٍ ۟اِسْتَنْقَذْتَنِىْ مِنْهُ يَا رَبَّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nWA LAA TARUDDANEE FEE SOO'INIS TANQADHTANEE MINHU YAA RABBAL A'ALAMEEN\nDo not return me to an evil from which You have rescued me, O Lord of the worlds.\nاَسْئَلُكَ اِيْمَانًا لَاۤ اَجَلَ لَهٗ دُوْنَ لِقَاۤئِكَ\nAS'ALUKA EEMAANAN LAA AJALA LAHOO DOONA LIQAA'IK\nI ask You for a faith that has no term short of meeting You,\nتُحْيِيْنِىْ وَتُمِيْتُنِىْ عَلَيْهِ وَتَبْعَثُنِىْ عَلَيْهِ اِذَا بَعَثْتَنِىْ\nTUHYEENEE WA TUMEETUNEE A'LAYHI WA TAB'ATHUNEE A'LAYHI IDHAA BA'ATHTANEE\nupon which You make me live and die, and upon which You raise me when You raise me.\nوَاَبْرِءْ قَلْبِىْ مِنَ الرِّيَاۤءِ وَالسُّمْعَةِ وَالشَّكِّ فِىْ دِيْنِكَ\nWA ABRI' QALBEE MINAR RIYAA'I WAS SUM'ATI WASH SHAKKI FEE DEENIK\nFree my heart from showing off, seeking fame, and doubt in Your religion.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَعْطِنِىْ نَصْرًا فِىْ دِيْنِكَ وَقُوَّةً فِىْ عِبَادَتِكَ وَفَهْمًا فِىْ خَلْقِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA A'TINEE NASRAN FEE DEENIKA WA QUWWATAN FEE I'BAADATIKA WA FAHMAN FEE KHALQIK\nO Allah, give me victory in Your religion, strength in Your worship, and understanding of Your creation,\nوَكِفْلَيْنِ مِنْ رَحْمَتِكَ وَبَيِّضْ وَجْهِىْ بِنُوْرِكَ\nWA KIFLAYNI MIN RAHMATIKA WA BAYYID WAJHEE BINOORIK\na double share of Your mercy; whiten my face with Your light,\nوَاجْعَلْ رَغْبَتِىْ فِيْمَا عِنْدَكَ\nWAJ'AL RAGHBATEE FEEMAA I'NDAK\nmake my desire be for what is with You,\nوَتَوَفَّنِىْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِكَ عَلٰى مِلَّتِكَ وَمِلَّةِ رَسُوْلِكَ\nWA TAWAFFANEE FEE SABEELIKA A'LAA MILLATIKA WA MILLATI RASOOLIK\nand take me in death in Your way, upon Your creed and the creed of Your Messenger.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنَ الْكَسَلِ وَالْهَرَمِ وَالْجُبْنِ وَالْبُخْلِ وَالْغَفْلَةِ وَالْقَسْوَةِ وَالْفَتْرَةِ وَالْمَسْكَنَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA MINAL KASALI WAL HARAMI WAL JUBNI WAL BUKHLI WAL GHAFLATI WAL QASWATI WAL FATRATI WAL MASKANAH\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, cowardice, miserliness, heedlessness, hardness of heart, slackness and wretchedness.\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِكَ يَا رَبِّ مِنْ نَفْسٍ لَا تَشْبَعُ\nWA A'OODHU BIKA YAA RABBI MIN NAFSIN LAA TASHBA'\nI seek refuge in You, O Lord, from a soul that is never satisfied,\nوَمِنْ قَلْبٍ لَا يَخْشَعُ\nWA MIN QALBIN LAA YAKHSHA'\nfrom a heart that is not humble,\nوَمِنْ دُعَاۤءٍ لَا يُسْمَعُ\nWA MIN DU'AA'IN LAA YUSMA'\nfrom a supplication that is not heard,\nوَمِنْ صَلٰوةٍ لَا تَنْفَعُ\nWA MIN SALAATIN LAA TANFA'\nand from a prayer that does not benefit.\nوَاُعِيْذُ بِكَ نَفْسِىْ وَاَهْلِىْ وَذُرِّيَّتِىْ مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ\nWA U'EEDHU BIKA NAFSEE WA AHLEE WA DHURRIYYATEE MINASH SHAYTAANIR RAJEEM\nI seek protection with You for myself, my family and my offspring from the accursed Satan.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُجِيْرُنِىْ مِنْكَ اَحَدٌ وَلَاۤ اَجِدُ مِنْ دُوْنِكَ مُلْتَحَدًا\nALLAAHUMMA INNAHOO LAA YUJEERUNEE MINKA AHADUN WA LAA AJIDU MIN DOONIKA MULTAHADAA\nO Allah, none can protect me from You, and I find no refuge other than You;\nفَلَا تَخْذُلْنِىْ وَلَا تَرُدَّنِىْ فِىْ هَلَكَةٍ وَلَا تَرُدَّنِىْ بِعَذَابٍ\nFALAA TAKHDHULNEE WA LAA TARUDDANEE FEE HALAKATIN WA LAA TARUDDANEE BI-A'DHAAB\nso do not forsake me, do not return me to perdition, and do not return me to punishment.\nاَسْئَلُكَ الثَّبَاتَ عَلٰى دِيْنِكَ وَالتَّصْدِيْقَ بِكِتَابِكَ وَاتِّبَاعَ رَسُوْلِكَ\nAS'ALUKATH THABAATA A'LAA DEENIKA WAT TASDEEQA BIKITAABIKA WATTIBAA'A RASOOLIK\nI ask You for steadfastness in Your religion, belief in Your Book, and following Your Messenger.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اذْكُرْنِىْ بِرَحْمَتِكَ وَلَا تَذْكُرْنِىْ بِخَطِيْئَتِىْ\nALLAAHUMMADH KURNEE BIRAHMATIKA WA LAA TADHKURNEE BIKHATEE'ATEE\nO Allah, remember me with Your mercy and do not remember me for my sins;\nوَتَقَبَّلْ مِنِّىْ وَزِدْنِىْ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ اِنِّىْۤ اِلَيْكَ رَاغِبٌ\nWA TAQABBAL MINNEE WA ZIDNEE MIN FADLIKA INNEE ILAYKA RAAGHIB\naccept from me and increase me from Your grace; I long for You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْ ثَوَابَ مَنْطِقِىْ وَثَوَابَ مَجْلِسِىْ رِضَاكَ عَنِّىْ\nALLAAHUMMAJ'AL THAWAABA MANTIQEE WA THAWAABA MAJLISEE RIDAAKA A'NNEE\nO Allah, make the reward of my speech and the reward of my sitting Your being pleased with me;\nوَاجْعَلْ عَمَلِىْ وَدُعَاۤئِىْ خَالِصًا لَكَ\nWAJ'AL A'MALEE WA DU'AA'EE KHAALISAN LAK\nmake my deeds and my supplication sincerely for You,\nوَاجْعَلْ ثَوَابِىَ الْجَنَّةَ بِرَحْمَتِكَ\nWAJ'AL THAWAABIYAL JANNATA BIRAHMATIK\nand make my reward Paradise, by Your mercy.\nوَاجْمَعْ لِىْ جَمِيْعَ مَا سَئَلْتُكَ\nWAJMA' LEE JAMEE'A MAA SA'ALTUK\nGather for me all that I have asked You,\nوَزِدْنِىْ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ اِنِّىْۤ اِلَيْكَ رَاغِبٌ\nWA ZIDNEE MIN FADLIKA INNEE ILAYKA RAAGHIB\nand increase me from Your grace; I long for You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ غَارَتِ النُّجُوْمُ وَنَامَتِ الْعُيُوْنُ\nALLAAHUMMA GHAARATIN NUJOOMU WA NAAMATIL U'YOON\nO Allah, the stars have set and the eyes have slept,\nوَاَنْتَ الْحَىُّ الْقَيُّوْمُ\nWA ANTAL HAYYUL QAYYOOM\nand You are the Ever-Living, the Self-Subsisting.\nلَا يُوَارِىْ مِنْكَ لَيْلٌ سَاجٍ وَلَا سَمَاۤءٌ ذَاتُ اَبْرَاجٍ\nLAA YUWAAREE MINKA LAYLUN SAAJIN WA LAA SAMAA'UN DHAATU ABRAAJ\nNothing is hidden from You by a still night, nor by a sky with constellations,\nوَلَاۤ اَرْضٌ ذَاتُ مِهَادٍ وَلَا بَحْرٌ لُجِّىٌ\nWA LAA ARDUN DHAATU MIHAADIN WA LAA BAHRUN LUJJIYY\nnor by an earth spread out, nor by a deep sea,\nوَلَا ظُلُمَاتٌ بَعْضُهَا فَوْقَ بَعْضٍ\nWA LAA ZULUMAATUN BA'DUHAA FAWQA BA'D\nnor by layers of darkness one above another.\nتُدْلِجُ الرَّحْمَةَ عَلٰى مَنْ تَشَاۤءُ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ\nTUDLIJUR RAHMATA A'LAA MAN TASHAA'U MIN KHALQIK\nYou let mercy travel through the night to whomever You will of Your creation;\nتَعْلَمُ خَاۤئِنَةَ الْاَعْيُنِ وَمَا تُخْفِىْ الصُّدُوْرُ\nTA'LAMU KHAA'INATAL A'YUNI WA MAA TUKHFIS SUDOOR\nYou know the treachery of the eyes and what the breasts conceal.\nاَشْهَدُ بِمَا شَهِدَتْ بِهٖ عَلٰى نَفْسِكَ وَشَهِدَتْ مَلَاۤئِكَتُكَ وَاُوْلُوْا الْعِلْمِ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ\nASH-HADU BIMAA SHAHIDAT BIHEE A'LAA NAFSIKA WA SHAHIDAT MALAA'IKATUKA WA OOLUL I'LMI LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTAL A'ZEEZUL HAKEEM\nI bear witness to what You have borne witness to about Yourself, and what Your angels and those endowed with knowledge have borne witness to: there is no god but You, the Mighty, the Wise.\nوَمَنْ لَمْ يَشْهَدْ عَلٰى مَا شَهِدْتَ عَلٰى نَفْسِكَ وَشَهِدَتْ مَلَاۤئِكَتُكَ وَاُوْلُوْا الْعِلْمِ فَاكْتُبْ شَهَادَتِىْ مَكَانَ شَهَادَتِهٖ\nWA MAN LAM YASH-HAD A'LAA MAA SHAHIDTA A'LAA NAFSIKA WA SHAHIDAT MALAA'IKATUKA WA OOLUL I'LMI FAKTUB SHAHAADATEE MAKAANA SHAHAADATIH\nAnd for whoever has not borne witness to what You, Your angels and those endowed with knowledge have borne witness to, write my testimony in place of his.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَنْتَ السَّلَامُ وَمِنْكَ السَّلَامُ\nALLAAHUMMA ANTAS SALAAMU WA MINKAS SALAAM\nO Allah, You are Peace and from You is peace.\nاَسْئَلُكَ يَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ اَنْ تَفُكَّ رَقَبَتِىْ مِنَ النّارِ\nAS'ALUKA YAA DHAL JALAALI WAL IKRAAMI AN TAFUKKA RAQABATEE MINAN NAAR\nI ask You, O Lord of Majesty and Honor, to free my neck from the Fire.",
    "Dua of Abu Dharr\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَسْاَلُكَ الْاَمْنَ وَالْاِيْمَانَ وَالتَّصْدِيْقَ بِنَبِيِّكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKAL AMNA WAL EEMAANA WAT TASDEEQA BINABIYYIK\nO Allah, I ask You for security, faith, and belief in Your Prophet,\nوَالْعَافِيَةَ مِنْ جَمِيْعِ الْبَلَاۤءِ\nWAL A'AFIYATA MIN JAMEE'IL BALAA'\nwell-being from every affliction,\nوَالشُّكْرَ عَلَى الْعَافِيَةِ وَالْغِنٰى عَنْ شِرَارِ النَّاسِ\nWASH SHUKRA A'LAL A'AFIYATI WAL GHINAA A'N SHIRAARIN NAAS\ngratitude for well-being, and independence from the wicked among people.",
    "Al-Dua al-Jami' (All-Inclusive Dua)\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the name of Allah, the All-Merciful, the All-Compassionate.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nI bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone, without partner,\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNA MUHAMMADAN A'BDUHOO WA RASOOLUH\nand I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.\nاٰمَنْتُ بِاللّٰهِ وَبِجَمِيْعِ رُسُلِهٖ وَبِجَمِيْعِ مَاۤ اُنْزِلَ بِهٖ عَلٰى جَمِيْعِ الرُّسُلِ\nAAMANTU BILLAAHI WA BIJAMEE'I RUSULIHEE WA BIJAMEE'I MAA UNZILA BIHEE A'LAA JAMEE'IR RUSUL\nI believe in Allah, in all His messengers, and in all that was sent down to all the messengers,\nوَاَنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ وَلِقَاۤئَهٗ حَقٌّ\nWA ANNA WA'DALLAAHI HAQQUN WA LIQAA'AHOO HAQQ\nand that Allah's promise is true and meeting Him is true.\nوَصَدَقَ اللّٰهُ وَبَلَّغَ الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ\nWA SADAQALLAAHU WA BALLAGHAL MURSALOON\nAllah has spoken the truth and the messengers have delivered the message.\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nWAL HAMDU LILLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN\nAll praise is for Allah, Lord of the worlds.\nوَسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ كُلَّمَا سَبَّحَ اللّٰهَ شَيْئٌ وَكَمَا يُحِبُّ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُسَبَّحَ\nWA SUBHAANALLAAHI KULLAMAA SABBAHALLAAHA SHAY'UN WA KAMAA YUHIBBULLAAHU AN YUSABBAH\nGlory be to Allah whenever anything glorifies Allah, and as Allah loves to be glorified;\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ كُلَّمَا حَمِدَ اللّٰهَ شَيْئٌ وَكَمَا يُحِبُّ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُحْمَدَ\nWAL HAMDU LILLAAHI KULLAMAA HAMIDALLAAHA SHAY'UN WA KAMAA YUHIBBULLAAHU AN YUHMAD\npraise be to Allah whenever anything praises Allah, and as Allah loves to be praised;\nوَلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ كُلَّمَا هَلَّلَ اللّٰهَ شَيْءٌ وَكَمَا يُحِبُّ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُهَلَّلَ\nWA LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU KULLAMAA HALLALALLAAHA SHAY'UN WA KAMAA YUHIBBULLAAHU AN YUHALLAL\nthere is no god but Allah whenever anything declares Allah's oneness, and as Allah loves His oneness to be declared;\nوَاللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ كُلَّمَا كَبَّرَ اللّٰهَ شَيْءٌ وَكَمَا يُحِبُّ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُكَبَّرَ\nWALLAAHU AKBARU KULLAMAA KABBARALLAAHA SHAY'UN WA KAMAA YUHIBBULLAAHU AN YUKABBAR\nand Allah is the Greatest whenever anything declares Allah's greatness, and as Allah loves His greatness to be declared.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَسْئَلُكَ مَفَاتِيْحَ الْخَيْرِ وَخَوَاتِيْمَهٗ وَسَوَابِغَهٗ وَفَوَاۤئِدَهٗ وَبَرَكَاتِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA MAFAATEEHAL KHAYRI WA KHAWAATEEMAHOO WA SAWAABIGHAHOO WA FAWAA'IDAHOO WA BARAKAATIH\nO Allah, I ask You for the keys of good, its seals, its abundance, its benefits and its blessings,\nوَمَا بَلَغَ عِلْمَهٗ عِلْمِىْ وَمَا قَصَرَ عَنْ اِحْصَاۤئِهٖ حِفْظِىْۤ\nWA MAA BALAGHA I'LMAHOO I'LMEE WA MAA QASARA A'N IHSAA'IHEE HIFZEE\nwhat my knowledge has reached and what my memory falls short of counting.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ انْهَجْ لِىْۤ اَسْبَابَ مَعْرِفَتِهٖ وَافْتَحْ لِىْۤ اَبْوَابَهٗ\nALLAAHUMMAN HAJ LEE ASBAABA MA'RIFATIHEE WAFTAH LEE ABWAABAH\nO Allah, open up for me the ways to knowing it and open its doors for me;\nوَغَشِّنِىْ بَرَكَاتِ رَحْمَتِكَ\nWA GHASHSHINEE BARAKAATI RAHMATIK\ncover me with the blessings of Your mercy,\nوَمُنَّ عَلَىَّ بِعِصْمَةٍ عَنِ الْاِزَالَةِ عَنْ دِيْنِكَ\nWA MUNNA A'LAYYA BI-I'SMATIN A'NIL IZAALATI A'N DEENIK\nand favor me with protection from swerving from Your religion.\nوَطَهِّرْ قَلْبِىْ مِنَ الشَّكِّ\nWA TAHHIR QALBEE MINASH SHAKK\nPurify my heart from doubt,\nوَلَا تَشْغَلْ قَلْبِىْ بِدُنْيَاىَ وَعَاجِلِ مَعَاشِىْ عَنْ اٰجِلِ ثَوَابِ اٰخِرَتِىْ\nWA LAA TASHGHAL QALBEE BIDUNYAAYA WA A'AJILI MA'AASHEE A'N AAJILI THAWAABI AAKHIRATEE\nand do not let my world and my immediate livelihood distract my heart from the deferred reward of my Hereafter.\nوَاشْغَلْ قَلْبِىْ بِحِفْظِ مَا لَا تَقْبَلُ مِنِّىْ جَهْلَهٗ\nWASHGHAL QALBEE BIHIFZI MAA LAA TAQBALU MINNEE JAHLAH\nOccupy my heart with preserving what You do not accept my ignorance of;\nوَذَلِّلْ لِكُلِّ خَيْرٍ لِسَانِىْ\nWA DHALLIL LIKULLI KHAYRIN LISAANEE\nmake my tongue submissive to every good;\nوَطَهِّرْ قَلْبِىْ مِنَ الرِّيَاۤءِ وَلَا تُجْرِهٖ فِىْ مَفَاصِلِىْ\nWA TAHHIR QALBEE MINAR RIYAA'I WA LAA TUJRIHEE FEE MAFAASILEE\npurify my heart from showing off and do not let it run through my joints;\nوَاجْعَلْ عَمَلِىْ خَالِصًا لَكَ\nWAJ'AL A'MALEE KHAALISAN LAK\nand make my deeds sincerely for You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنَ الشَّرِّ وَاَنْوَاعِ الْفَوَاحِشِ كُلِّهَا ظَاهِرِهَا وَبَاطِنِهَا وَغَفَلَاتِهَا\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA MINASH SHARRI WA ANWAA'IL FAWAAHISHI KULLIHAA ZAAHIRIHAA WA BAATINIHAA WA GHAFALAATIHAA\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You from evil and from all kinds of indecency, the open and the hidden of them and their heedless moments,\nوَجَمِيْعِ مَا يُرِيْدُنِىْ بِهِ الشَّيْطَانُ الرَّجِيْمُ وَمَا يُرِيْدُنِىْ بِهِ السُّلْطَانُ الْعَنِيْدُ\nWA JAMEE'I MAA YUREEDUNEE BIHISH SHAYTAANUR RAJEEMU WA MAA YUREEDUNEE BIHIS SULTAANUL A'NEED\nand from all that the accursed Satan and the obstinate ruler intend against me,\nمِمَّاۤ اَحَطْتَ بِعِلْمِهٖ وَاَنْتَ الْقَادِرُ عَلٰى صَرْفِهٖ عَنِّىْۤ\nMIMMAA AHATTA BI-I'LMIHEE WA ANTAL QAADIRU A'LAA SARFIHEE A'NNEE\nof what Your knowledge encompasses, and You have power to turn it away from me.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ طَوَارِقِ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ وَزَوَابِعِهِمْ وَبَوَاۤئِقِهِمْ وَمَكَايِدِهِمْ وَمَشَاهِدِ الْفَسَقَةِ مِنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA MIN TAWAARIQIL JINNI WAL INSI WA ZAWAABI'IHIM WA BAWAA'IQIHIM WA MAKAAYIDIHIM WA MASHAAHIDIL FASAQATI MINAL JINNI WAL INS\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You from the night-visitors of jinn and men, their whirlwinds, their calamities, their schemes, and the gatherings of the corrupt among jinn and men;\nوَاَنْ اُسْتَزَلَّ عَنْ دِيْنِىْ فَتَفْسُدَ عَلَىَّ اٰخِرَتِىْ\nWA AN USTAZALLA A'N DEENEE FATAFSUDA A'LAYYA AAKHIRATEE\nand from being made to slip from my religion so that my Hereafter is ruined for me,\nوَاَنْ يَكُوْنَ ذٰلِكَ مِنْهُمْ ضَرَرًا عَلَىَّ فِىْ مَعَايِشِىْ\nWA AN YAKOONA DHAALIKA MINHUM DARARAN A'LAYYA FEE MA'AAYISHEE\nand from that being a harm to me from them in my livelihood,\nاَوْ يَعْرِضَ بَلَاۤءٌ يُصِيْبُنِىْ مِنْهُمْ لَا قُوَّةَ لِىْ بِهٖ وَلَا صَبْرَ لِىْ عَلَى احْتِمَالِهِ\nAW YA'RIDA BALAA'UN YUSEEBUNEE MINHUM LAA QUWWATA LEE BIHEE WA LAA SABRA LEE A'LAH TIMAALIH\nor an affliction coming upon me from them which I have no strength for and no patience to bear.\nفَلَا تَبْتَلِيَنِّىْ يَاۤ اِلٰهِىْ بِمُقَاسَاتِهٖ فَيَمْنَعُنِىْ ذٰلِكَ عَنْ ذِكْرِكَ وَيَشْغَلُنِىْ عَنْ عِبَادَتِكَ\nFALAA TABTALIYANNEE YAA ILAAHEE BIMUQAASAATIHEE FAYAMNA'UNEE DHAALIKA A'N DHIKRIKA WA YASHGHALUNEE A'N I'BAADATIK\nSo do not try me, O my God, with enduring it, so that it keeps me from remembering You and distracts me from worshipping You.\nاَنْتَ الْعَاصِمُ الْمَانِعُ الدَّافِعُ الْوَاقِىْ مِنْ ذٰلِكَ كُلِّهٖ\nANTAL A'ASIMUL MAANI'UD DAAFI'UL WAAQEE MIN DHAALIKA KULLIH\nYou are the Protector, the Preventer, the Repeller, the Guard against all that.\nاَسْئَلُكَ اللّٰهُمَّ الرَّفَاهِيَةَ فِىْ مَعِيْشَتِىْ مَاۤ اَبْقَيْتَنِىْ\nAS'ALUKALLAAHUMMAR RAFAAHIYATA FEE MA'EESHATEE MAA ABQAYTANEE\nI ask You, O Allah, for ease in my livelihood as long as You keep me alive,\nمَعِيْشَةً اَقْوٰى بِهَا عَلٰى طَاعَتِكَ وَاَبْلُغُ بِهَا رِضْوَانَكَ\nMA'EESHATAN AQWAA BIHAA A'LAA TAA'ATIKA WA ABLUGHU BIHAA RIDWAANAK\na livelihood by which I gain strength to obey You and attain Your good pleasure,\nوَاَصِيْرُ بِهَاۤ اِلٰى دَارِ الْحَيَوَانِ غَدًا\nWA ASEERU BIHAA ILAA DAARIL HAYAWAANI GHADAA\nand by which I reach the Abode of true life tomorrow.\nوَلَا تَرْزُقْنِىْ رِزْقًا يُطْغِيْنِىْ وَلَا تَبْتَلِيَنِّىْ بِفَقْرٍ اَشْقٰى بِهٖ مُضَيَّقًا عَلَىَّ\nWA LAA TARZUQNEE RIZQAN YUTGHEENEE WA LAA TABTALIYANNEE BIFAQRIN ASHQAA BIHEE MUDAYYAQAN A'LAYY\nDo not give me a sustenance that makes me transgress, nor try me with a poverty that makes me wretched and straitened.\nاَعْطِنِىْ حَظًّا وَافِرًا فِىْۤ اٰخِرَتِىْ وَمَعَاشًا وَاسِعًا هَنِيْۤئًا مَرِیْۤئًا فِىْ دُنْيَاىَ\nA'TINEE HAZZAN WAAFIRAN FEE AAKHIRATEE WA MA'AASHAN WAASI'AN HANEE'AN MAREE'AN FEE DUNYAAY\nGive me an abundant share in my Hereafter and a wide, pleasant and wholesome livelihood in my world.\nوَلَا تَجْعَلِ الدُّنْيَا عَلَىَّ سِجْنًا وَلَا تَجْعَلْ فِرَاقَهَا عَلَىَّ حُزْنًا\nWA LAA TAJ'ALID DUNYAA A'LAYYA SIJNAN WA LAA TAJ'AL FIRAAQAHAA A'LAYYA HUZNAA\nDo not make this world a prison for me, nor make parting from it a grief for me.\nاَجِرْنِىْ مِنْ فِتْنَتِهَا وَاجْعَلْ عَمَلِىْ فِيْهَا مَقْبُوْلًا وَسَعْيِىْ فِيْهَا مَشْكُوْرًا\nAJIRNEE MIN FITNATIHAA WAJ'AL A'MALEE FEEHAA MAQBOOLAN WA SA'YEE FEEHAA MASHKOORAA\nShelter me from its trials, and make my deeds in it accepted and my striving in it appreciated.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَمَنْ اَرَادَنِىْ بِسُوْۤءٍ فَاَرِدْهُ بِمِثْلِهٖ وَمَنْ كَادَنِىْ فِيْهَا فَكِدْهُ\nALLAAHUMMA WA MAN ARAADANEE BISOO'IN FA-ARID-HU BIMITHLIHEE WA MAN KAADANEE FEEHAA FAKID-H\nO Allah, whoever intends evil for me, intend the same for him, and whoever plots against me in it, plot against him.\nوَاصْرِفْ عَنِّىْ هَمَّ مَنْ اَدْخَلَ عَلَىَّ هَمَّهٗ\nWASRIF A'NNEE HAMMA MAN ADKHALA A'LAYYA HAMMAH\nTurn away from me the worry of whoever brings his worry upon me,\nوَامْكُرْ بِمَنْ مَكَرَ بِىْ فَاِنَّكَ خَيْرُ الْمَاكِرِيْنَ\nWAMKUR BIMAN MAKARA BEE FA-INNAKA KHAYRUL MAAKIREEN\nand scheme against whoever schemes against me, for You are the best of schemers.\nوَافْقَاْ عَنِّىْ عُيُوْنَ الْكَفَرَةِ الظَّلَمَةِ وَالطُّغَاةِ الْحَسَدَةِ\nWAFQA' A'NNEE U'YOONAL KAFARATIZ ZALAMATI WAT TUGHAATIL HASADAH\nBlind to me the eyes of the unbelievers, the wrongdoers, the tyrants and the envious.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَاَنْزِلْ عَلَىَّ مِنْكَ السَّكِيْنَةَ وَاَلْبِسْنِىْ دِرْعَكَ الْحَصِيْنَةَ\nALLAAHUMMA WA ANZIL A'LAYYA MINKAS SAKEENATA WA ALBISNEE DIR'AKAL HASEENAH\nO Allah, send down upon me tranquility from You, and clothe me in Your fortified armor;\nوَاحْفَظْنِىْ بِسِرِّكَ الْوَاقِىْ وَجَلِّلْنِىْ عَافِيَتَكَ النَّافِعَةَ\nWAHFAZNEE BISIRRIKAL WAAQEE WA JALLILNEE A'AFIYATAKAN NAAFI'AH\nguard me with Your protecting secret, and cover me with Your beneficial well-being;\nوَصَدِّقْ قَوْلِىْ وَفِعَالِىْ وَبَارِكْ لِىْ فِىْ وَلَدِىْ وَاَهْلِىْ وَمَالِىْ\nWA SADDIQ QAWLEE WA FI'AALEE WA BAARIK LEE FEE WALADEE WA AHLEE WA MAALEE\nconfirm my words and my deeds, and bless me in my children, my family and my wealth.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ مَا قَدَّمْتُ وَمَاۤ اَخَّرْتُ وَمَاۤ اَغْفَلْتُ وَمَا تَعَمَّدْتُ وَمَا تَوَانَيْتُ وَمَاۤ اَعْلَنْتُ وَمَاۤ اَسْرَرْتُ\nALLAAHUMMA MAA QADDAMTU WA MAA AKHKHARTU WA MAA AGHFALTU WA MAA TA'AMMADTU WA MAA TAWAANAYTU WA MAA A'LANTU WA MAA ASRART\nO Allah, whatever I have done before and after, whatever I have neglected and done on purpose, whatever I have been slack in, and whatever I have done openly and in secret,\nفَاغْفِرْ لِىْ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nFAGHFIR LEE YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nforgive me, O Most Merciful of the merciful.",
    "For Sustenance, Life & Forgiveness\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَوْسِعْ عَلَىَّ فِىْ رِزْقِىْ وَامْدُدْ لِىْ فِىْ عُمْرِىْ وَاغْفِرْ لِىْ ذَنْبِىْ\nALLAAHUMMA AWSI' A'LAYYA FEE RIZQEE WAMDUD LEE FEE U'MREE WAGHFIR LEE DHANBEE\nO Allah, widen my sustenance, lengthen my life, and forgive my sin;\nوَاجْعَلْنِىْ مِمَّنْ تَنْتَصِرُ بِهٖ لِدِيْنِكَ وَلَا تَسْتَبْدِلْ بِى غَيْرِىْ\nWAJ'ALNEE MIMMAN TANTASIRU BIHEE LIDEENIKA WA LAA TASTABDIL BEE GHAYREE\nmake me one of those through whom You support Your religion, and do not replace me with another.",
    "Dua Ya Man Yashkur al-Yasir\nيَا مَنْ يَشْكُرُ الْيَسِيْرَ وَيَعْفُوْ عَنِ الْكَثِيْرِ وَهُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ\nYAA MAN YASHKURUL YASEERA WA YA'FOO A'NIL KATHEERI WA HUWAL GHAFOORUR RAHEEM\nO He Who appreciates the little and pardons the much, and He is the All-Forgiving, the All-Merciful,\nاِغْفِرْ لِىَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِىْ ذَهَبَتْ لَذَّتُهَا وَبَقِيَتْ تَبِعَتُهَا\nIGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE DHAHABAT LADHDHATUHAA WA BAQIYAT TABI'ATUHAA\nforgive me the sins whose pleasure has gone and whose consequences remain.",
    "Dua Ya Nur Ya Quddus\nيَا نُوْرُ يَا قُدُّوْسُ يَاۤ اَوَّلَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَيَاۤ اٰخِرَ الْاٰخِرِيْنَ يَا رَحْمٰنُ يَا رَحِيْمُ\nYAA NOORU YAA QUDDOOSU YAA AWWALAL AWWALEENA WA YAA AAKHIRAL AAKHIREENA YAA RAHMAANU YAA RAHEEM\nO Light, O Holy One, O First of the first, O Last of the last, O All-Merciful, O All-Compassionate,\nاِغْفِرْ لِىَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِىْ تُغَيِّرُ النِّعَمَ\nIGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TUGHAYYIRUN NI'AM\nforgive me the sins that change blessings,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِىَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِىْ تُحِلُّ النِّقَمَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TUHILLUN NIQAM\nforgive me the sins that bring down punishments,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِىَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِىْ تَهْتِكُ الْعِصَمَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TAHTIKUL I'SAM\nforgive me the sins that tear apart protection,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِىَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِىْ تُنْزِلُ الْبَلَاۤءَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TUNZILUL BALAA'\nforgive me the sins that bring down affliction,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِىَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِىْ تُدِيْلُ الْاَعْدَاۤءَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TUDEELUL A'DAA'\nforgive me the sins that give enemies the upper hand,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِىَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِىْ تُعَجِّلُ الْفَنَاۤءَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TU'AJJILUL FANAA'\nforgive me the sins that hasten annihilation,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِىَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِىْ تَقْطَعُ الرَّجَاۤءَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TAQTA'UR RAJAA'\nforgive me the sins that cut off hope,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِىَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِىْ تُظْلِمُ الْهَوَاۤءَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TUZLIMUL HAWAA'\nforgive me the sins that darken the air,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِىَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِىْ تَكْشِفُ الْغِطَاۤءَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TAKSHIFUL GHITAA'\nforgive me the sins that lift the veil,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِىَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِىْ تَرُدُّ الدُّعَاۤءَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TARUDDUD DU'AA'\nforgive me the sins that hold back supplication,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِىَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِىْ تَرُدُّ غَيْثَ السَّمَاۤءِ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TARUDDU GHAYTHAS SAMAA'\nand forgive me the sins that hold back the rain of the sky.",
    "Dua Ya Uddati fi Kurbati\nيَا عُدَّتِىْ فِىْ كُرْبَتِىْ وَيَا صَاحِبِىْ فِىْ شِدَّتِىْ\nYAA U'DDATEE FEE KURBATEE WA YAA SAAHIBEE FEE SHIDDATEE\nO my Provision in my distress, O my Companion in my hardship,\nوَيَا وَلِىّٖ فِىْ نِعْمَتِىْ وَيَا غِيَاثِىْ فِىْ رَغَبَتِىْ\nWA YAA WALIYYEE FEE NI'MATEE WA YAA GHIYAATHEE FEE RAGHABATEE\nO my Guardian in my blessing, O my Helper in my desire.",
    "Dua of Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.)\nاَللّٰهُمَّ كَتَبْتَ الْاٰثَارَ وَعَلِمْتَ الْاَخْبَارَ وَاطَّلَعْتَ عَلَى الْاَسْرَارِ\nALLAAHUMMA KATABTAL AATHAARA WA A'LIMTAL AKHBAARA WATTALA'TA A'LAL ASRAAR\nO Allah, You have recorded the traces, known the reports, and seen the secrets,\nفَحُلْتَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَ الْقُلُوْبِ\nFAHULTA BAYNANAA WA BAYNAL QULOOB\nand You have come between us and the hearts;\nفَالسِّرُّ عِنْدَكَ عَلَانِيَةٌ وَالْقُلُوْبُ اِلَيْكَ مُفْضَاةٌ\nFAS SIRRU I'NDAKA A'LAANIYATUN WAL QULOOBU ILAYKA MUFDAAH\nfor the secret is open before You, and hearts are laid bare to You.\nوَاِنَّمَاۤ اَمْرُكَ لِشَيْئٍ اِذَا اَرَدْتَهٗ اَنْ تَقُوْلَ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُ\nWA INNAMAA AMRUKA LISHAY'IN IDHAA ARADTAHOO AN TAQOOLA LAHOO KUN FAYAKOON\nYour command, when You will a thing, is only to say to it \"Be\", and it is.\nفَقُلْ بِرَحْمَتِكَ لِطَاعَتِكَ اَنْ تَدْخُلَ فِىْ كُلِّ عُضْوٍ مِنْ اَعْضَاۤئِىْ وَلَا تُفَارِقَنِىْ حَتّٰىۤ اَلْقَاكَ\nFAQUL BIRAHMATIKA LITAA'ATIKA AN TADKHULA FEE KULLI U'DWIN MIN A'DAA'EE WA LAA TUFAARIQANEE HATTAA ALQAAK\nSo by Your mercy, command obedience to You to enter every limb of mine and not leave me until I meet You;\nوَقُلْ بِرَحْمَتِكَ لِمَعْصِيَتِكَ اَنْ تَخْرُجَ مِنْ كُلِّ عُضْوٍ مِنْ اَعْضَاۤئِىْ فَلَا تَقْرُبَنِىْ حَتّٰىۤ اَلْقَاكَ\nWA QUL BIRAHMATIKA LIMA'SIYATIKA AN TAKHRUJA MIN KULLI U'DWIN MIN A'DAA'EE FALAA TAQRUBANEE HATTAA ALQAAK\nand by Your mercy, command disobedience to You to leave every limb of mine and not come near me until I meet You.\nوَارْزُقْنِىْ مِنَ الدُّنْيَا وَزَهِّدْنِىْ فِيْهَا وَلَا تَزْوِهَا عَنِّىْ وَرَغْبَتِىْ فِيْهَا يَاۤ رَحْمٰنُ\nWARZUQNEE MINAD DUNYAA WA ZAHHIDNEE FEEHAA WA LAA TAZWIHAA A'NNEE WA RAGHBATEE FEEHAA YAA RAHMAAN\nProvide for me from this world and make me renounce it; do not withhold it from me while my desire is in it, O All-Merciful.",
    "Dua al-Hamdu Lillahi Waliyy al-Hamd\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَلِىِّ الْحَمْدِ وَاَهْلِهٖ وَمُنْتَهَاهُ وَمَحَلِّهٖ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHI WALIYYIL HAMDI WA AHLIHEE WA MUNTAHAAHU WA MAHALLIH\nPraise be to Allah, the Master of praise, its Worthy One, its Utmost End and its Abode.\nاَخْلَصَ مَنْ وَحَّدَهٗ وَاهْتَدٰى مَنْ عَبَدَهٗ\nAKHLASA MAN WAHHADAHOO WAHTADAA MAN A'BADAH\nSincere is he who declares His oneness, guided is he who worships Him,\nوَفَازَ مَنْ اَطَاعَهٗ وَاَمِنَ الْمُعْتَصِمُ بِهٖ\nWA FAAZA MAN ATAA'AHOO WA AMINAL MU'TASIMU BIH\nsuccessful is he who obeys Him, and safe is he who holds fast to Him.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ يَا ذَا الْجُوْدِ وَالْمَجْدِ وَالثَّنَاۤءِ الْجَمِيْلِ وَالْحَمْدِ\nALLAAHUMMA YAA DHAL JOODI WAL MAJDI WATH THANAA'IL JAMEELI WAL HAMD\nO Allah, O Lord of generosity, glory, beautiful laudation and praise,\nاَسْئَلُكَ مَسْئَلَةَ مَنْ خَضَعَ لَكَ بِرَقَبَتِهٖ وَرَغَمَ لَكَ اَنْفُهٗ وَعَفَّرَ لَكَ وَجْهَهٗ\nAS'ALUKA MAS'ALATA MAN KHADA'A LAKA BIRAQABATIHEE WA RAGHAMA LAKA ANFUHOO WA A'FFARA LAKA WAJHAH\nI ask You as one asks who bows his neck before You, whose nose is humbled for You, who lays his face in the dust for You,\nوَذَلَّلَ لَكَ نَفْسَهٗ وَفَاضَتْ مِنْ خَوْفِكَ دُمُوْعُهٗ وَتَرَدَّدَتْ عَبْرَتُهٗ\nWA DHALLALA LAKA NAFSAHOO WA FAADAT MIN KHAWFIKA DUMOO'UHOO WA TARADDADAT A'BRATUH\nwho abases himself before You, whose tears flow out of fear of You, whose sobs come again and again,\nوَاعْتَرَفَ لَكَ بِذُنُوبِهٖ وَفَضَحَتْهُ عِنْدَكَ خَطِيْئَتُهٗ وَشَاَنَتْهُ عِنْدَكَ جَرِيْرَتُهٗ\nWA'TARAFA LAKA BIDHUNOOBIHEE WA FADAHAT-HU I'NDAKA KHATEE'ATUHOO WA SHA'ANAT-HU I'NDAKA JAREERATUH\nwho confesses his sins to You, whose wrongdoing has disgraced him before You and whose offense has shamed him before You,\nفَضَعُفَتْ عِنْدَ ذٰلِكَ قُوَّتُهٗ وَقَلَّتْ حِيْلَتُهٗ وَانْقَطَعَتْ عَنْهُ اَسْبَابُ خَدَايِعِهٖ وَاضْمَحَلَّ عَنْهُ كُلُّ بَاطِلٍ\nFADA'UFAT I'NDA DHAALIKA QUWWATUHOO WA QALLAT HEELATUHOO WANQATA'AT A'NHU ASBAABU KHADAAYI'IHEE WADMAHALLA A'NHU KULLU BAATIL\nso that his strength has weakened, his means have dwindled, the means of his deceptions are cut off from him, and every falsehood has vanished from him,\nوَاَلْجَاَتْهُ ذُنُوْبُهٗ اِلٰى ذُلِّ مَقَامِهٖ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ وَخُضُوْعِهٖ لَدَيْكَ وَابْتِهَالِهِ اِلَيْكَ\nWA ALJA'AT-HU DHUNOOBUHOO ILAA DHULLI MAQAAMIHEE BAYNA YADAYKA WA KHUDOO'IHEE LADAYKA WABTIHAALIHEE ILAYK\nand his sins have driven him to the abasement of standing before You, to humility in Your presence and to pleading with You.\nاَسْئَلُكَ اللّٰهُمَّ سُؤَالَ مَنْ هُوَ بِمَنْزِلَتِهٖ اَرْغَبُ اِلَيْكَ كَرَغْبَتِهٖ وَاَتَضَرَّعُ اِلَيْكَ كَتَضَرُّعِهٖ وَاَبْتَهِلُ اِلَيْكَ كَاَشَدِّ ابْتِهَالِهِ\nAS'ALUKALLAAHUMMA SU'AALA MAN HUWA BIMANZILATIHEE ARGHABU ILAYKA KARAGHBATIHEE WA ATADARRA'U ILAYKA KATADARRU'IHEE WA ABTAHILU ILAYKA KA-ASHADDIB TIHAALIH\nI ask You, O Allah, as one in his position asks: I long for You as he longs, I implore You as he implores, and I plead with You with his most intense pleading.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَارْحَمِ اسْتِكَانَةَ مَنْطِقِىْ وَذُلَّ مَقَامِىْ وَمَجْلِسِىْ وَخُضُوْعِىْ اِلَيْكَ بِرَقَبَتِىْ\nALLAAHUMMA FARHAMIS TIKAANATA MANTIQEE WA DHULLA MAQAAMEE WA MAJLISEE WA KHUDOO'EE ILAYKA BIRAQABATEE\nO Allah, have mercy on the humility of my speech, the abasement of my standing and sitting, and my bowing my neck to You.\nاَسْئَلُكَ اللّٰهُمَّ الْهُدٰى مِنَ الضَّلَالَةِ وَالْبَصِيْرَةَ مِنَ الْعَمٰى وَالرُّشْدَ مِنَ الْغِوَايَةِ\nAS'ALUKALLAAHUMMAL HUDAA MINAD DALAALATI WAL BASEERATA MINAL A'MAA WAR RUSHDA MINAL GHIWAAYAH\nI ask You, O Allah, for guidance out of misguidance, insight out of blindness, and right conduct out of error.\nوَاَسْئَلُكَ اللّٰهُمَّ اَكْثَرَ الْحَمْدِ عِنْدَ الرَّخَاۤءِ وَاَجْمَلَ الصَّبْرِ عِنْدَ الْمُصِيْبَةِ وَاَفْضَلَ الشُّكْرِ عِنْدَ مَوْضِعِ الشُّكْرِ وَالتَّسْلِيْمَ عِنْدَ الشُّبُهَاتِ\nWA AS'ALUKALLAAHUMMA AKTHARAL HAMDI I'NDAR RAKHAA'I WA AJMALAS SABRI I'NDAL MUSEEBATI WA AFDALASH SHUKRI I'NDA MAWDI'ISH SHUKRI WAT TASLEEMA I'NDASH SHUBUHAAT\nI ask You, O Allah, for abundant praise in ease, the most beautiful patience in calamity, the best gratitude where gratitude is due, and submission in matters of doubt.\nوَاَسْئَلُكَ الْقُوَّةَ فِىْ طَاعَتِكَ وَالضَّعْفَ عَنْ مَعْصِيَتِكَ وَالْهَرَبَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْكَ وَالتَّقَرُّبَ اِلَيْكَ رَبِّ لِتَرْضٰى\nWA AS'ALUKAL QUWWATA FEE TAA'ATIKA WAD DA'FA A'N MA'SIYATIKA WAL HARABA ILAYKA MINKA WAT TAQARRUBA ILAYKA RABBI LITARDAA\nI ask You for strength in obeying You, weakness in disobeying You, flight to You from You, and drawing near to You, my Lord, so that You are pleased,\nوَالتَّحَرِّىَ لِكُلِّ مَا يُرْضِيْكَ عَنِّىْ فِىْ اِسْخَاطِ خَلْقِكَ اِلْتِمَاسًا لِرِضَاكَ\nWAT TAHARRIYA LIKULLI MAA YURDEEKA A'NNEE FEE ISKHAATI KHALQIKA ILTIMAASAN LIRIDAAK\nand striving for all that pleases You with me, even at the anger of Your creation, seeking Your good pleasure.\nرَبِّ مَنْ اَرْجُوْهُ اِنْ لَمْ تَرْحَمْنِىْ اَوْ مَنْ يَعُوْدُ عَلَىَّ اِنْ اَقْصَيْتَنِىْ\nRABBI MAN ARJOOHU IN LAM TARHAMNEE AW MAN YA'OODU A'LAYYA IN AQSAYTANEE\nMy Lord, whom shall I hope in if You do not have mercy on me? Who will be kind to me if You send me away?\nاَوْ مَنْ يَنْفَعُنِىْ عَفْوُهٗ اِنْ عَاقَبْتَنِىْ اَوْ مَنْ اٰمُلُ عَطَايَاهُ اِنْ حَرَمْتَنِىْ\nAW MAN YANFA'UNEE A'FWUHOO IN A'AQABTANEE AW MAN AAMULU A'TAAYAAHU IN HARAMTANEE\nWhose pardon will benefit me if You punish me? Whose gifts shall I hope for if You deprive me?\nاَوْ مَنْ يَمْلِكُ كَرَامَتِىْۤ اِنْ اَهَنْتَنِىْ اَوْ مَنْ يَضُرُّنِىْ هَوَانُهٗ اِنْ اَكْرَمْتَنِىْ\nAW MAN YAMLIKU KARAAMATEE IN AHANTANEE AW MAN YADURRUNEE HAWAANUHOO IN AKRAMTANEE\nWho can grant me honor if You humiliate me? Whose contempt can harm me if You honor me?\nرَبِّ مَاۤ اَسْوَءَ فِعْلِىْ وَاَقْبَحَ عَمَلِىْ وَاَقْسٰى قَلْبِىْ وَاَطْوَلَ اَمَلِىْ وَاَقْصَرَ اَجَلِىْ وَاَجْرَاَنِىْ عَلٰى عِصْيَانِ مَنْ خَلَقَنِىْ\nRABBI MAA ASWA'A FI'LEE WA AQBAHA A'MALEE WA AQSAA QALBEE WA ATWALA AMALEE WA AQSARA AJALEE WA AJRA'ANEE A'LAA I'SYAANI MAN KHALAQANEE\nMy Lord, how evil is my conduct, how ugly my deeds, how hard my heart, how long my hope, how short my term, and how bold I am in disobeying the One Who created me!\nرَبِّ وَمَاۤ اَحْسَنَ بَلَاۤئَكَ عِنْدِىْ وَاَظْهَرَ نَعْمَاۤئَكَ عَلَىَّ\nRABBI WA MAA AHSANA BALAA'AKA I'NDEE WA AZHARA NA'MAA'AKA A'LAYY\nMy Lord, how good is Your trial of me and how manifest Your blessings upon me!\nكَثُرَتْ عَلَىَّ مِنْكَ النِّعَمُ فَمَاۤ اُحْصِيْهَا وَقَلَّ مِنِّىْ الشُّكْرُ فِيْمَاۤ اَوْلَيْتَنِيْهِ\nKATHURAT A'LAYYA MINKAN NI'AMU FAMAA UHSEEHAA WA QALLA MINNISH SHUKRU FEEMAA AWLAYTANEEH\nYour blessings upon me have multiplied so that I cannot count them, while my gratitude for what You have granted me has been little.\nفَبَطِرْتُ بِالنِّعَمِ وَتَعَرَّضْتُ لِلنِّقَمِ وَسَهَوْتُ عَنِ الذِّكْرِ\nFABATIRTU BIN NI'AMI WA TA'ARRADTU LIN NIQAMI WA SAHAWTU A'NIDH DHIKR\nI have grown insolent with the blessings, exposed myself to punishments, and become heedless of remembrance;\nوَرَكِبْتُ الْجَهْلَ بَعْدَ الْعِلْمِ وَجُزْتُ مِنَ الْعَدْلِ اِلَى الظُّلْمِ وَجَاوَزْتُ الْبِرَّ اِلَى الْاِثْمِ\nWA RAKIBTUL JAHLA BA'DAL I'LMI WA JUZTU MINAL A'DLI ILAZ ZULMI WA JAAWAZTUL BIRRA ILAL ITHM\nI have taken to ignorance after knowledge, passed from justice to injustice, and gone beyond righteousness to sin,\nوَصِرْتُ اِلَى اللَّهْوِ مِنَ الْخَوْفِ وَالْحُزْنِ\nWA SIRTU ILAL LAHWI MINAL KHAWFI WAL HUZN\nand I have turned to amusement away from fear and sorrow.\nفَمَاۤ اَصْغَرَ حَسَنَاتِىْ وَاَقَلَّهَا فِىْ كَثْرَةِ ذُنُوْبِىْ وَاَعْظَمَهَا عَلٰى قَدْرِ صِغَرِ خَلْقِىْ وَضَعْفِ رُكْنِىْ\nFAMAA ASGHARA HASANAATEE WA AQALLAHAA FEE KATHRATI DHUNOOBEE WA A'ZAMAHAA A'LAA QADRI SIGHARI KHALQEE WA DA'FI RUKNEE\nHow small are my good deeds and how few among my many sins, and how great my sins in proportion to the smallness of my frame and the weakness of my support!\nرَبِّ وَمَاۤ اَطْوَلَ اَمَلِىْ فِىْ قِصَرِ اَجَلِىْ وَاَقْصَرَ اَجَلِىْ فِىْ بُعْدِ اَمَلِىْ\nRABBI WA MAA ATWALA AMALEE FEE QISARI AJALEE WA AQSARA AJALEE FEE BU'DI AMALEE\nMy Lord, how long is my hope despite the shortness of my term, and how short my term compared to the reach of my hope,\nوَمَاۤ اَقْبَحَ سَرِيْرَتِىْ فِىْ عَلَانِيَتِىْ\nWA MAA AQBAHA SAREERATEE FEE A'LAANIYATEE\nand how ugly is my inward state compared to my outward one!\nرَبِّ لَا حُجَّةَ لِىْۤ اِنِ احْتَجَجْتُ وَلَا عُذْرَ لِىْ اِنِ اعْتَذَرْتُ\nRABBI LAA HUJJATA LEE INIH TAJAJTU WA LAA U'DHRA LEE INI' TADHART\nMy Lord, I have no argument if I argue, and no excuse if I make excuses,\nوَلَا شُكْرَ عِنْدِىْۤ اِنِ ابْتَلَيْتُ وَاُوْلِيْتُ اِنْ لَمْ تُعِنِّىْ عَلٰى شُكْرِ مَا اَوْلَيْتَ\nWA LAA SHUKRA I'NDEE INIB TALAYTU WA OOLEETU IN LAM TU'INNEE A'LAA SHUKRI MAA AWLAYT\nand no gratitude with me if I am tried and favored, unless You help me to thank You for what You have granted.\nرَبِّىْ مَاۤ اَخَفَّ مِيْزَانِىْ غَدًا اِنْ لَمْ تُرَجِّحْهُ وَاَزَلَّ لِسَانِىْ اِنْ لَمْ تُثَبِّتْهُ وَاَسْوَدَ وَجْهِىْۤ اِنْ لَمْ تُبَيِّضْهُ\nRABBEE MAA AKHAFFA MEEZAANEE GHADAN IN LAM TURAJJIH-HU WA AZALLA LISAANEE IN LAM TUTHABBIT-HU WA ASWADA WAJHEE IN LAM TUBAYYID-H\nMy Lord, how light my scale will be tomorrow if You do not make it heavy, how my tongue will slip if You do not make it firm, and how black my face will be if You do not whiten it!\nرَبِّ كَيْفَ لِىْ بِذُنُوْبِىَ الَّتِىْ سَلَفَتْ مِنِّىْ قَدْ هُدَّتْ لَهَاۤ اَرْكَانِىْ\nRABBI KAYFA LEE BIDHUNOOBIYAL LATEE SALAFAT MINNEE QAD HUDDAT LAHAA ARKAANEE\nMy Lord, what am I to do with my past sins, by which my pillars have been shattered?\nرَبِّ كَيْفَ اَطْلُبُ شَهَوَاتِ الدُّنْيَا وَاَبْكِىْ عَلٰى خَيْبَتِىْ فِيْهَا وَلَاۤ اَبْكِىْ وَتَشْتَدُّ حَسَرَاتِىْ عَلٰى عِصْيَانِىْ وَتَفْرِيْطِىْ\nRABBI KAYFA ATLUBU SHAHAWAATID DUNYAA WA ABKEE A'LAA KHAYBATEE FEEHAA WA LAA ABKEE WA TASHTADDU HASARAATEE A'LAA I'SYAANEE WA TAFREETEE\nMy Lord, how can I pursue the desires of this world and weep over my failure in it, yet not weep, nor feel intense regret, over my disobedience and my negligence?\nرَبِّ دَعَتْنِىْ دَوَاعِىْ الدُّنْيَا فَاَجَبْتُهَا سَرِيْعًا وَرَكَنْتُ اِلَيْهَا طَاۤئِعًا\nRABBI DA'ATNEE DAWAA'ID DUNYAA FA-AJABTUHAA SAREE'AN WA RAKANTU ILAYHAA TAA'I'AA\nMy Lord, the callers of this world called me and I answered them quickly and inclined to them willingly;\nوَدَعَتْنِىْ دَوَاعِىْ الْاٰخِرَةِ فَتَثَبَّطْتُ عَنْهَا وَاَبْطَاْتُ فِى الْاِجَابَةِ وَالْمُسَارَعَةِ اِلَيْهَا\nWA DA'ATNEE DAWAA'IL AAKHIRATI FATATHABBATTU A'NHAA WA ABTA'TU FIL IJAABATI WAL MUSAARA'ATI ILAYHAA\nthe callers of the Hereafter called me and I held back from them and was slow in answering them and hastening to them,\nكَمَا سَارَعْتُ اِلٰى دَوَاعِىْ الدُّنْيَا وَحُطَامِهَا الْهَامِدِ وَهَشِيْمِهَا الْبَاۤئِدِ وَسَرَابِهَا الذَّاهِبِ\nKAMAA SAARA'TU ILAA DAWAA'ID DUNYAA WA HUTAAMIHAL HAAMIDI WA HASHEEMIHAL BAA'IDI WA SARAABIHADH DHAAHIB\nas I hastened to the callers of this world, its withered debris, its perishing stubble and its fleeting mirage.\nرَبِّ خَوَّفْتَنِىْ وَشَوَّقْتَنِىْ وَاحْتَجَجْتَ عَلَىَّ بِرِقِّىْ وَتَكَفَّلْتَ لِىْ بِرِزْقِىْ\nRABBI KHAWWAFTANEE WA SHAWWAQTANEE WAHTAJAJTA A'LAYYA BIRIQQEE WA TAKAFFALTA LEE BIRIZQEE\nMy Lord, You made me fear and You made me long, You argued against me by my servitude, and You guaranteed my sustenance;\nفَاَمِنْتُ خَوْفَكَ وَتَثَبَّطْتُ عَنْ تَشْوِيْقِكَ وَلَمْ اَتَّكِلْ عَلٰى ضَمَانِكَ وَتَهَاوَنْتُ بِاحْتِجَاجِكَ\nFA-AMINTU KHAWFAKA WA TATHABBATTU A'N TASHWEEQIKA WA LAM ATTAKIL A'LAA DAMAANIKA WA TAHAAWANTU BIHTIJAAJIK\nyet I felt safe from Your threat, held back from Your encouragement, did not rely on Your guarantee, and made light of Your argument.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَاجْعَلْ اَمْنِىْ مِنْكَ فِىْ هٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا خَوْفًا وَحَوِّلْ تَثَبُّطِىْ شَوْقًا وَتَهَاوُنِىْ بِحُجَّتِكَ فَرَقًا مِنْكَ\nALLAAHUMMA FAJ'AL AMNEE MINKA FEE HAADHIHID DUNYAA KHAWFAN WA HAWWIL TATHABBUTEE SHAWQAN WA TAHAAWUNEE BIHUJJATIKA FARAQAN MINK\nO Allah, then turn my feeling of safety from You in this world into fear, my holding back into longing, and my making light of Your argument into awe of You;\nثُمَّ رَضِّنِىْ بِمَا قَسَمْتَ لِىْ مِنْ رِزْقِكَ يَا كَرِيْمُ\nTHUMMA RADDINEE BIMAA QASAMTA LEE MIN RIZQIKA YAA KAREEM\nthen make me content with the sustenance You have allotted me, O Generous One.\nاَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الْعَظِيْمِ رِضَاكَ عِنْدَ السُّخْطَةِ وَالْفُرْجَةَ عِنْدَ الْكُرْبَةِ وَالنُّوْرَ عِنْدَ الظُّلْمَةِ وَالْبَصِيْرَةَ عِنْدَ تَشَبُّهِ الْفِتْنَةِ\nAS'ALUKA BISMIKAL A'ZEEMI RIDAAKA I'NDAS SUKHTATI WAL FURJATA I'NDAL KURBATI WAN NOORA I'NDAZ ZULMATI WAL BASEERATA I'NDA TASHABBUHIL FITNAH\nI ask You by Your Great Name for Your good pleasure at times of anger, relief at times of distress, light in darkness, and insight when trials are confusing.\nرَبِّ اجْعَلْ جُنَّتِىْ مِنْ خَطَايَاىَ حَصِيْنَةً وَدَرَجَاتِىْ فِى الْجِنَانِ رَفِيْعَةً وَاَعْمَالِىْ كُلَّهَا مُتَقَبَّلَةً وَحَسَنَاتِىْ مُضَاعَفَةً زَاكِيَةً\nRABBIJ'AL JUNNATEE MIN KHATAAYAAYA HASEENATAN WA DARAJAATEE FIL JINAANI RAFEE'ATAN WA A'MAALEE KULLAHAA MUTAQABBALATAN WA HASANAATEE MUDAA'AFATAN ZAAKIYAH\nMy Lord, make my shield against my sins strong, my ranks in the gardens high, all my deeds accepted, and my good deeds multiplied and pure.\nاَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنَ الْفِتَنِ كُلِّهَا مَا ظَهَرَ مِنْهَا وَمَا بَطَنَ\nA'OODHU BIKA MINAL FITANI KULLIHAA MAA ZAHARA MINHAA WA MAA BATAN\nI seek refuge in You from all trials, the open and the hidden,\nوَمِنْ رَفِيْعِ الْمَطْعَمِ وَالْمَشْرَبِ\nWA MIN RAFEE'IL MAT'AMI WAL MASHRAB\nfrom luxurious food and drink,\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ مَاۤ اَعْلَمُ وَمِنْ شَرِّ مَا لَاۤ اَعْلَمُ\nWA MIN SHARRI MAA A'LAMU WA MIN SHARRI MAA LAA A'LAM\nfrom the evil of what I know and the evil of what I do not know.\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ اَنْ اَشْتَرِىَ الْجَهْلَ بِالْعِلْمِ وَالْجَفَا بِالْحِلْمِ وَالْجَوْرَ بِالْعَدْلِ وَالْقَطِيْعَةَ بِالْبِرِّ وَالْجَزَعَ بِالصَّبْرِ\nWA A'OODHU BIKA MIN AN ASHTARIYAL JAHLA BIL I'LMI WAL JAFAA BIL HILMI WAL JAWRA BIL A'DLI WAL QATEE'ATA BIL BIRRI WAL JAZA'A BIS SABR\nAnd I seek refuge in You from trading knowledge for ignorance, forbearance for harshness, justice for tyranny, kindness for severing ties, and patience for impatience,\nاَوِ الْهُدٰى بِالضَّلَالَةِ اَوِ الْكُفْرَ بِالْاِيْمَانِ\nAWIL HUDAA BID DALAALATI AWIL KUFRA BIL EEMAAN\nor guidance for misguidance, or faith for disbelief."
