  "merits": "Dua of Insistence: This supplication is reported to be the supplication of insistence.\n\nAllahumma Imla' Qalbi: Ibn Abi-Ya’fur, the prominent and trustworthy narrator, is reported to have said that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) used to say this supplication. Shaykh al-Tusi, in Misbah al-Mutahajjid, has referred to it to be said immediately after the fourth unit of the Night Prayer. As for al-Majlisi (the compiler of Bihar al-Anwar), he reported Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) to have recommended saying it in the one-unit Watr Prayer (which is performed after the eight-unit Night Prayer and the two-unit Shaf’ Prayer at the early dawn).\n\nDua of Abu Dharr: This supplication is reportedly ascribed to Abu-Dharr. About it, Archangel Gabriel is reported to have said to the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), “This supplication is well known by the inhabitants of the heavens.”\n\nAl-Dua al-Jami': Abu-Hamzah is reported to have said: I have received this supplication from Imam al-Baqir (a.s.), who used to describe it as the all-inclusive supplication.\n\nFor sustenance, life and forgiveness: Muhammad ibn Muslim is reported to have quoted Imam al-Baqir (a.s.) as advising saying this supplication.\n\nYa Man Yashkur al-Yasir: Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have used to say this supplication.\n\nYa Nur Ya Quddus: Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is also reported to have used to say this supplication.\n\nYa Uddati fi Kurbati: This supplication is also reported from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.).\n\nDua of Amir al-Mu'minin: Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) added: This is the supplication of Imam ‘Ali Amir al-Mu’minin (a.s.).\n\nAl-Hamdu Lillahi Waliyy al-Hamd: ‘Ali ibn Ibrahim has reported on the authority of his father on the authority of Ibn Mahbub on the authority of ‘Ala’ ibn Ruzayn on the authority of ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Sayyabah, who said: Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) gave me this supplication."
